**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| **Medium** | HARES uses solar constant = 1367 W/m² (WMO 1982), not the modern IAU/NREL SPA value of 1361.1 W/m². Systematic +0.43% overestimate (~6 W/m² at perihelion/aphelion). |
| **Low** | Spencer 1971 eccentricity formula correct — matches pvlib's `'spencer'` method exactly. More accurate than EnergyPlus's 2-term AVSC. |
| **Low** | Test comment claims pvlib parity but pvlib now defaults to 1366.1, not 1367. Documentation inaccuracy. |
| **Info** | EnergyPlus uses multiple solar constants (1367/1355/1353); HARES's single-value approach is appropriate for its scope. |
